q-316753" :question/problem "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-6)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316753/field-1" "q-316753/field-2" "q-316753/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316753"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7921/selection/f137086f26f25d30428df6d4b7ac8f3f39419de9e1d12f7e984534b0e774a94c" :answer/id #uuid "fe1f879a-709a-589a-97e4-74a95bce36f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7921/selection/60eabb7b6b8b0c223082542677334b4abf8af887ba5da52471f6292ba2fe63a2" :answer/id #uuid "ceb8c988-7f92-5c04-b601-54a5e38af944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7921/selection/8d4faa1cdb1c0a0bb4ad58eb2dcb78e790e97d51119258f6aed1d11334d229b6" :answer/id #uuid "87321a7e-0fc4-5e5b-a9f6-da27b92468cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7921/selection/9ce2fab67e736420dc95c2a974aecc99cc08713c35cbafe2c56e69e004cfd04c" :answer/id #uuid "c485af0d-eb54-5bae-ab4e-fbe45131fe3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7921/selection/b7f069f2967cee40887dcd358cd461f7fd11ade916f382518e1424e5349a752a" :answer/id #uuid "3459b861-aeb7-55f5-b0c9-27620c047db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7921/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3dfd702-1b82-588f-8458-2013f9b01d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7921/selection/9ce2fab67e736420dc95c2a974aecc99cc08713c35cbafe2c56e69e004cfd04c" :answer-field/choices ["q-7921/selection/f137086f26f25d30428df6d4b7ac8f3f39419de9e1d12f7e984534b0e774a94c" "q-7921/selection/60eabb7b6b8b0c223082542677334b4abf8af887ba5da52471f6292ba2fe63a2" "q-7921/selection/8d4faa1cdb1c0a0bb4ad58eb2dcb78e790e97d51119258f6aed1d11334d229b6" "q-7921/selection/9ce2fab67e736420dc95c2a974aecc99cc08713c35cbafe2c56e69e004cfd04c" "q-7921/selection/b7f069f2967cee40887dcd358cd461f7fd11ade916f382518e1424e5349a752a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7921" :question/id #uuid "9e0cdcdd-62cd-58bc-822f-b8a4f1afe9a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-7921" :question/problem "Calculate ${E}^{-1}$, where\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $E$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(E)=4\\cdot 7-8\\cdot 3=4\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E{E}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {E}^{-1}E & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7921/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7921"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11725"] :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=6\\cdot 4-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)=0,$ we conclude that $B$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-1)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 5=-10.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ do not have an inverse." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-71937/selection/27ead39b22315899a97d19d41807fad901038aea957324f0c89ba36f126544db" :answer/id #uuid "293a000b-5fa3-57f5-9c73-c304496bfc14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71937/selection/233efd06028b4b12dae76bb4cabec3ea02c2f67c9e3ee2646051c190df73ca18" :answer/id #uuid "479ede7d-ca69-5627-b741-68a5088f3990" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$T$ and $V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71937/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" :answer/id #uuid "bc8c0e80-c30c-50b3-82ad-9bbd5045fc90" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71937/selection/6c5d8db382b33f30f332b189fe1fe2973356c5fdb6f69748c83cf4a47a8bf0ab" :answer/id #uuid "5f05dd50-60ac-56b8-8d96-1693f5941558" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71937/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" :answer/id #uuid "4a83cf5c-2492-5e7d-bd1f-81cb45d8045e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71937/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75efd0d7-75e1-5283-b402-be9d95bd287d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71937/selection/6c5d8db382b33f30f332b189fe1fe2973356c5fdb6f69748c83cf4a47a8bf0ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-71937/selection/27ead39b22315899a97d19d41807fad901038aea957324f0c89ba36f126544db" "q-71937/selection/233efd06028b4b12dae76bb4cabec3ea02c2f67c9e3ee2646051c190df73ca18" "q-71937/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" "q-71937/selection/6c5d8db382b33f30f332b189fe1fe2973356c5fdb6f69748c83cf4a47a8bf0ab" "q-71937/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71937" :question/id #uuid "ff070848-777f-5635-9918-6da54f4ec8b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-71937" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $T$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=3\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-15)=-3.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $V$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(V)=6\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(V)=0,$ we conclude that $V$ is not invertible. Since $V$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $V$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $V$ is singular." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71937/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71937"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127751/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "db222ce2-d658-59e8-abed-720804bd2f85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127751/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "4ebdb491-448d-58e9-9879-1b62216ed7af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127751/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "9ffc3da3-6ece-5f07-aa43-96a827f4751d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127751/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "417850f7-e746-50ba-baca-15037850a3d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127751/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "fa4a2fb7-63c1-5e6f-9be6-7787e63f53af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127751/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "66c0f296-846d-563e-b7ef-ec9210792f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127751/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer-field/choices ["q-127751/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-127751/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" "q-127751/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-127751/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-127751/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127751" :question/id #uuid "8bc7e218-c432-5c7d-93cb-660cd4ed939b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127751" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-3)\\cdot (3)=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127751/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71968/selection/10fcf7552088b1c2c25c33b4e90dcdcdabe32cbf83a3e6e18c7dcd301487e4e5" :answer/id #uuid "fa2f4b1a-4076-5d23-92af-36d061da630b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=\\pm 5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71968/selection/ff052473a04d990b28ad92ba9bbf8d50d73e6bf43c452e149cc97692a407ebb9" :answer/id #uuid "abdcb851-7d2c-5f10-a66e-50ee99c035c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=\\pm 6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71968/selection/4ced7721048df3b9428002dea8464ee26c85a4074b277ddcf7bd86118c70348a" :answer/id #uuid "5189922d-eb94-5d49-8fc8-c514cadda484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71968/selection/e0d3c606ed5ce35d86e4a9e8a0f6c1cd1d194f6772dae8009ce0d54eec26aadb" :answer/id #uuid "06b8493a-99ff-5e6c-9a77-45c69605c0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71968/selection/715c3b5132f9313e292199c539ba50720533a5932320a9d54c18a1fd68a22846" :answer/id #uuid "42467990-ad8c-56f7-89f2-e087fe3bf2c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71968/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8638e24-5ed1-52ea-8e76-4fdcef0463c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71968/selection/10fcf7552088b1c2c25c33b4e90dcdcdabe32cbf83a3e6e18c7dcd301487e4e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-71968/selection/10fcf7552088b1c2c25c33b4e90dcdcdabe32cbf83a3e6e18c7dcd301487e4e5" "q-71968/selection/ff052473a04d990b28ad92ba9bbf8d50d73e6bf43c452e149cc97692a407ebb9" "q-71968/selection/4ced7721048df3b9428002dea8464ee26c85a4074b277ddcf7bd86118c70348a" "q-71968/selection/e0d3c606ed5ce35d86e4a9e8a0f6c1cd1d194f6772dae8009ce0d54eec26aadb" "q-71968/selection/715c3b5132f9313e292199c539ba50720533a5932320a9d54c18a1fd68a22846"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71968" :question/id #uuid "8c22c847-601a-5a56-9c84-b8ca008f9f6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-71968" :question/problem "If $H=[\\begin{aligned}5 & c \\\\ c & 5\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $H$ is singular if and only if $det(H)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & =5\\cdot 5-c\\cdot c \\\\  & =25-{c}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25-{c}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =25 \\\\ c & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $c$ are $c=\\pm 5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71968/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71968"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316784/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer/id #uuid "20dea9c5-a46a-5cf9-a2e4-7aa6a62e9727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316784/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "e3707f8a-5ad7-5365-8eae-901a4d71871c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316784/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f63b0cec-8348-5835-a6df-4b735dd0bcc4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316784/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer-field/choices ["q-316784/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" "q-316784/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316784" :question/id #uuid "66c05155-e66f-5d77-9b4e-130629dd787b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316784" :question/problem "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -x+1 \\\\ 5 & 2x+7\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(-3)\\cdot (2x+7)-5\\cdot (-x+1) \\\\  & =-6x-21+5x-5 \\\\  & =-x-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-26 & =0 \\\\ -x & =26 \\\\ x & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316784/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316828/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "b75012e3-e492-5792-9719-1d397d71cf66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316828/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3c73af9-51b6-5091-b134-07564ff2febe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316828/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-316828/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316828/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1520c08b-c044-52a0-bba9-fde2eed71cec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316828/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "79908c2f-632b-513d-aa7a-fed9ae5536d8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316828/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-316828/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316828" :question/id #uuid "8b310642-ede6-5a4f-a56c-989f0c39c332" :question/math-academy-id "q-316828" :question/problem "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & x-40 \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+1)\\cdot (-x)-(x-40)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-x-x+40 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-2x+40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-2x+40 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+x-20) & =0 \\\\ -2(x-4)(x+5) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316828/field-1" "q-316828/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316783/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "9cb3c9e2-3c64-577f-aeb1-5d5e914b8b41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316783/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffa74d1b-4335-56bb-aab7-44ba0eb0ffe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316783/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-316783/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316783" :question/id #uuid "5443d517-7df6-5344-80b9-17b5b74831e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316783" :question/problem "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}5x & -1 \\\\ 6x-8 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(5x)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (6x-8) \\\\  & =10x+6x-8 \\\\  & =16x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16x-8 & =0 \\\\ 16x & =8 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316783/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316783"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
